@Xichen96 — re-reviewed exact head `c1ac463c72f461c3e73ce33b55e296015d7219e0` and its integration with the current `master`.

All previously raised concerns are addressed:

- teardown now stops the responder and flushes only the responder-owned neighbor entries;
- `ip neigh flush to ... dev ...` is idempotent for absent entries while still exposing invalid interface/namespace failures;
- both helpers materialize `ip_intf_pairs`, so list, generator, and `filter` callers are safe;
- the WoL fixtures pass their owned pairs through teardown;
- the current DHCPv6 downstream-relay caller passes the VLAN SVI and route-owned responder tuple correctly.

The targeted invalidation avoids disturbing unrelated FDB/ARP/NDP state while preserving the responder refresh lifecycle. DCO, EasyCLA, static checks, security checks, and all impacted-area CI jobs are green.

**LGTM — approving this revision.**

@StormLiangMS Final head `35e0136c6d2e32cee961fa1d16a96ca295e10f75` addresses all three points:

- teardown stops the responder and flushes only responder-owned neighbors;
- targeted `ip neigh flush to ... dev ...` is idempotent when the entry is absent but still fails visibly for an invalid interface/namespace;
- the shared helpers materialize `ip_intf_pairs`, while WoL passes generators instead of redundant lists.

